zune-jpeg fuzz: decode_incremental: compare DNL output at the resolved height

For a DNL image (SOF height 0) `output_buffer_size()` reports the size for
`max_height` until the scan has resolved the DNL height, so the harness
allocates its incremental output buffer at max height (4096 rows) while the
one-shot `decode()` returns exactly width x DNL-height pixels. Once
`decode_into` succeeds the harness compared the whole max-height buffer and
asserted on the length ("incremental output length diverges from one-shot
decode", e.g. 36864 vs 36). Truncate the buffer to `output_buffer_size()`
after the scan, as the decoder documents for DNL images; for all other
images the size is unchanged. Harness bug in upstream's fuzz target, not a
decoder bug (with the truncation all 162 crashers of this kind compare equal).

Not fixed upstream as of zune-image 2cdbbf5.
Upstream: none found (fuzz target added in #389).

diff --git a/crates/zune-jpeg/fuzz/fuzz_targets/decode_incremental.rs b/crates/zune-jpeg/fuzz/fuzz_targets/decode_incremental.rs
index 29489ff0..fa508f02 100644
--- a/crates/zune-jpeg/fuzz/fuzz_targets/decode_incremental.rs
+++ b/crates/zune-jpeg/fuzz/fuzz_targets/decode_incremental.rs
@@ -236,6 +236,13 @@ fuzz_target!(|data: &[u8]| {
         return;
     }
 
+    // DNL images (SOF height 0) need an output buffer sized for the
+    // configured maximum height; once the scan resolves the DNL height only
+    // `output_buffer_size()` bytes are image data.
+    if let Some(size) = decoder.output_buffer_size() {
+        out.truncate(size);
+    }
+
     // Compare against ground truth: one-shot succeeded AND incremental
     // finished with full data visibility for the scan.
     if let Some(expected_pixels) = oneshot_pixels {
